Day 2 – Git Pull, Branching & Merging 

What I Did: 
 - Synced local repo with GitHub
   . Created a new folder (learning-notes) directly in GitHub
   . When I checked locally, the folder was missing
   . Understood that git pull is required to bring remote changes into the local repository
 - Created and worked with branches
   . Created a new branch for test-branch for learning
   . Understood that branches are local by default and don’t appear on GitHub unless pushed
 - Faced upstream error and fixed it
   . When I tried to push test-branch, got an error saying no upstream branch exists
   . Used: git push -u origin test-branch
   . Learned that: -u sets the upstream & After this, git push works normally 
 - Planned feature-based development using branches
   . calculator.sh in main already had addition and subtraction
   . Decided to: Add multiplication and division in test-branch & Merge the branch into main
   . Learned that this is the correct and safe way to develop new features
  - Understood merging workflow 
   . Learned the correct merge process 
   . Understood that: main should stay stable & Feature branches are merged only after work is complete
